{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "3ff22083-135a-4fb7-9eec-50e343d55c86",
    "name": "Parking · spot-service",
    "description": "spot-service — verificado contra `release` el 2026-07-27.\n\nTodos los endpoints de `SpotRestAdapter` estan implementados. Base path `/v1/spots`.\n\nTipos validos de `type`: `CAR`, `CAR_PMR`, `MOTORBIKE`.\nEstados de `status` en la respuesta: `AVAILABLE`, `OCCUPIED`, `UNAVAILABLE`.\n\nRequiere JWT: todos los endpoints estan protegidos con `@PreAuthorize` (`SecurityConfig` sin `@Profile`, aplica siempre). Corre \"0. Auth\" antes que el resto para rellenar `accessToken` (colección con auth Bearer a nivel de colección).\n\nAvisos sobre el contrato:\n- `PATCH /{id}/status` **sí cambia el estado**: recibe `SpotStatusRequest` (campo\n  `status`) y delega en `UpdateSpotStatusUseCase` (RN-10). Solo admite\n  AVAILABLE <-> UNAVAILABLE; pedir OCCUPIED por aqui da 409.\n- `POST /occupy` recibe `SpotOccupyRequest` (`{\"vehicleType\": ...}`) y devuelve\n  `SpotResponse`. `vehicleType` es el campo canonico; `type` se acepta solo como\n  alias temporal para no acoplar el orden de despliegue con stay-service.\n- `GET /v1/spots/availability` existe y devuelve `AvailabilityResponse`\n  (`type`/`available`/`availableCount`/`totalCount`). Sin el parametro `type` da 400.\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Obtener token (admin.test)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{keycloakTokenUrl}}",
              "host": [
                "{{keycloakTokenUrl}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "POST al token endpoint de Keycloak con `grant_type=password`. `parking-frontend` es publico con `directAccessGrantsEnabled: true`, asi que no hace falta `client_secret`.\n\nGuarda `access_token` en la variable de environment `accessToken`, que consume el resto de la coleccion via el auth Bearer de nivel de coleccion. Ejecutar esta request antes que las demas (o correr toda la coleccion de arriba a abajo).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "key": "grant_type",
                  "value": "password"
                },
                {
                  "key": "client_id",
                  "value": "{{keycloakClientId}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "username",
                  "value": "{{adminUser}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "password",
                  "value": "{{adminPassword}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "scope",
                  "value": "openid"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('devuelve access_token', () => pm.expect(body.access_token).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.environment.set('accessToken', body.access_token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Crear plaza",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrlSpot}}/v1/spots",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrlSpot}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "spots"
          ]
        },
        "description": "POST /v1/spots -> 201 Created. Body: `{\"type\": \"CAR\"}`.\n\nGuarda el id en `spotId`.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"type\": \"{{vehicleType}}\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.environment.set('spotId', body.id);",
              "pm.test('nace AVAILABLE', () => pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('AVAILABLE'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Listar plazas",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrlSpot}}/v1/spots",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrlSpot}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "spots"
          ]
        },
        "description": "GET /v1/spots -> 200 con todas las plazas."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('devuelve un array', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an('array'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Obtener plaza por id",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrlSpot}}/v1/spots/{{spotId}}",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrlSpot}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "spots",
            "{{spotId}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "GET /v1/spots/{id} -> 200."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Ocupar plaza (RN-01)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrlSpot}}/v1/spots/occupy",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrlSpot}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "spots",
            "occupy"
          ]
        },
        "description": "POST /v1/spots/occupy -> 200 con la plaza asignada.\n\nBody: `{\"vehicleType\": \"CAR\"}` — `vehicleType` es el campo canonico de `SpotOccupyRequest`. `type` se acepta como alias temporal (`@JsonAlias(\"type\")`) solo para no acoplar el orden de despliegue con stay-service; se retira cuando stay-service migre.\n\nEs el endpoint que stay-service necesita en el check-in. Si no queda ninguna plaza libre de ese tipo, aqui se materializa **RN-01 (parking completo)**.\n\n> Ojo: `StaySpotClientAdapter.occupySpot` llama a esta ruta con **PATCH**, no con POST -> hoy recibe 405 y el check-in nunca ocupa plaza. Ver README, seccion 'Bugs conocidos'.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"vehicleType\": \"{{vehicleType}}\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.environment.set('spotId', body.id);",
              "pm.test('queda OCCUPIED', () => pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('OCCUPIED'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Liberar plaza",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrlSpot}}/v1/spots/{{spotId}}/release",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrlSpot}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "spots",
            "{{spotId}}",
            "release"
          ]
        },
        "description": "POST /v1/spots/{id}/release -> 200. Sin body.\n\nEs la compensacion que ejecuta el check-in (IN-25) si falla al guardar la estancia despues de haber ocupado la plaza."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('vuelve a AVAILABLE', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('AVAILABLE'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Actualizar plaza (tipo)",
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrlSpot}}/v1/spots/{{spotId}}",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrlSpot}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "spots",
            "{{spotId}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "PUT /v1/spots/{id} -> 200. Body: `{\"type\": ...}`. Solo cambia el tipo de plaza.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"type\": \"MOTORBIKE\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('tipo actualizado', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().type).to.eql('MOTORBIKE'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Marcar plaza como UNAVAILABLE (HU-05 CA5)",
      "request": {
        "method": "PATCH",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrlSpot}}/v1/spots/{{spotId}}/status",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrlSpot}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "spots",
            "{{spotId}}",
            "status"
          ]
        },
        "description": "`PATCH /v1/spots/{id}/status` -> 200. Recibe `SpotStatusRequest` (`{\"status\": ...}`) y cambia el estado de verdad (RN-10).\n\nSolo admite AVAILABLE <-> UNAVAILABLE. Pedir OCCUPIED por aqui devuelve 409: para ocupar esta `POST /v1/spots/occupy`.\n\nOJO cross-repo: `StaySpotClientAdapter.updateSpotStatus` sigue mandando `{\"type\": ...}` y por tanto recibe un 400. Hoy no lo llama ningun caso de uso de stay-service.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"UNAVAILABLE\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('la plaza queda UNAVAILABLE', () => pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('UNAVAILABLE'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Consultar disponibilidad (HU-03)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrlSpot}}/v1/spots/availability?type=CAR",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrlSpot}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "spots",
            "availability"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "type",
              "value": "CAR"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "`GET /v1/spots/availability?type=` -> 200 con `AvailabilityResponse`.\n\nSolo lee, no reserva nada: para ocupar esta `POST /v1/spots/occupy`.\nRN-10: las plazas UNAVAILABLE no cuentan como disponibles, asi que `availableCount` puede ser 0 con `totalCount` > 0.\n\nSin el parametro `type` responde 400."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('responde el tipo consultado', () => pm.expect(body.type).to.eql('CAR'));",
              "pm.test('trae los contadores', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(body.availableCount).to.be.a('number');",
              "    pm.expect(body.totalCount).to.be.a('number');",
              "});",
              "pm.test('available es coherente con availableCount', () => pm.expect(body.available).to.eql(body.availableCount > 0));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  }
}
